course: dictionary
lesson: 9255
title: Soundly: three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. The clues around soundly tell you which one to choose. «Toad slept very soundly, and no amount of shaking could rouse him.» Sleeping soundly means sleeping deeply and well, so deeply that nothing wakes you.
explain: Look at the words around it. «The visitors were soundly beaten.» Soundly does not mean quietly here. Ask: what word would fit? Completely fits, so soundly means completely or heavily, and the visitors lost by a lot.
explain: In an idea, soundly means sensible and reliable. «Her essay was soundly argued» means the reasons were good and well thought out, like a house built on solid foundations.
fact: Soundly is an adverb: it tells you how something is done.
fact: «Soundly» means deeply and well, as in «sleep soundly».
fact: «Soundly» means completely or heavily, as in «soundly beaten».
fact: «Soundly» means in a sensible, reliable or well-built way, as in «soundly made» or «soundly argued».
fact: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If the sentence still makes sense, you have chosen the right meaning.
exercise: «She slept soundly all night and did not hear the storm.» What does soundly mean here? | Hardly at all | *Deeply and well, without waking | Slowly, on tiptoe | Loudly and angrily
exercise: «The visitors were soundly beaten 6-0.» What does soundly mean here? | Almost, but not quite | Quietly | *Completely, by a big margin | Politely
exercise: «Her essay was soundly argued, with evidence for every point.» What does soundly mean here? | Without any sound at all | *In a sensible, well-reasoned way | Loudly and clearly | Sleepily
test: «The bridge was soundly built and has stood for a hundred years.» What does soundly mean here? | Noisy and loud | Briefly, for a short time | Sadly and slowly | *Well-built and reliable
test: Mum asks, «Did you sleep soundly?» What is she asking? | Whether you were noisy in bed | *Whether you slept deeply and well | Whether you slept in the car | Whether you woke up early
exam: Which sentence uses soundly to mean completely or heavily? | *The home team was soundly beaten | The old chair was soundly made | The idea was soundly argued | The baby slept soundly in her cot
